    "title": "Arizona Diamondbacks' Eduardo Rodriguez shines in WBC for Venezuela",
    "text": "DIAMONDBACKSDiamondbacks' Eduardo Rodriguez shines in World Baseball Classic Nick PiecoroArizona RepublicUpdated March 17, 2026, 8:00 p.m. MTKeep WatchingDiamondbacks left-hander Eduardo Rodriguez came up big under the bright lights Tuesday, March 17, shutting down a potent Team USA lineup at the World Baseball Classic championship game in Miami.Venezuela scored once on a Eugenio Juarez double in the ninth inning to take a 3-2 victory.Rodriguez pitched into the fifth inning for Venezuela, handing a 2-0 lead to his bullpen after firing 4 1/3 innings of one-hit ball, walking one and striking out four.Expected to be one of the Diamondbacks' starting pitchers to open this season, Rodriguez had just a 5.02 ERA in 29 starts last year. He is 94-66 with a 4.19 ERA over 10 big-league seasons.He turns 33 next month.Baseball HQ: Projections and analysis to power your fantasy baseball season.Rodriguez fanned New York Yankees slugger Aaron Judge, a three-time American League MVP, twice; Minnesota Twins two-time All-Star Byron Buxton once; and the Phillies' three-time All-Star Kyle Schwarber once.Diamondbacks' Zac Gallen hits Opening Day better, stronger, faster Arkansas, Arizona Sweet 16 features fabulous freshmen 'Really good test.' Diamondbacks open 2026 MLB season at Dodger Stadium 7 Arizona State football players who should return from injury in 2026(This story has been updated to add new information.)Don’t Miss These Tax Deductions & CreditsTurboTax | AdAdLearn MoreUndoOoni's Compact Gas Oven is a Game Changer–See WhyOoni Koda 2 - Portable, easy to use and now available with a rotating stoneOoni Pizza Ovens | AdAdLearn MoreUndoYour Refund is Calling! IRS E-File is OpenTurboTax | AdAdLearn MoreUndoNew $45 Fee: What No REAL ID Means for YouIf you still don’t have a REAL ID, here’s what the new $45 airport fee means for your domestic travel, the documents you’ll need to fly within the US, and how to obtain your REAL IDAAA | AdAdUndoSharp Memory After 60 Has Been L